WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.080
Since appearing in 1984, Freddy Krueger has
become an iconic horror villain.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.000
But how did he go from a child killer in a
grimy Christmas sweater to Jason Voorhees'

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.500
puppeteer?

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.440
Here's the breakdown of the entire, original
Nightmare on Elm Street story.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.420
Our first real introduction to Freddy Krueger
comes in the form of a dream that high schooler

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.080
Tina has one terrible night.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.520
She later shares the experience with her friends,
Nancy, Glen, and Rod, who have all been having

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.360
the same dreams about the same man.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.460
It's soon revealed that the monster in their
dreams was once a human child killer who became

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.070
the target of the town's parents after the
legal system failed to bring him to justice.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.720
"But he can't get you now.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.680
He's dead, honey, because mommy killed him."

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:47.940
Somehow, Krueger figured out how to live on
in the dream world, and now he wants to murder

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.900
the children of the parents who killed him.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.780
Luckily, Nancy eventually defeats him after
dragging him into the real world.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:58.319
After their confrontation, Nancy walks outside
her house, and all seems well.

00:00:58.319 --> 00:01:03.289
Her friends are alive, and everything is sunshine
and roses … until the car suddenly turns

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:05.930
into a Freddy-mobile and traps everyone inside.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:11.250
Five years later, in Freddy's Revenge, a kid
named Jesse and his family move into Nancy's

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:16.360
old house on Elm Street, and an entirely new
cast of characters are tormented by Freddy.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:20.880
Jesse's dreams of Freddy are a little different
from Nancy's, in that Jesse never really finds

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.900
himself in any danger of being killed.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.760
But when he and his friend, Lisa, find Nancy's
old diary, he realizes exactly who he's up

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:28.260
against.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.920
In order to stay awake, Jesse starts to wander
around town at night.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:37.159
He winds up in an S&amp;M bar, where his leather-clad
gym coach catches him drinking a beer and

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.100
takes him back to the school to punish him.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:43.580
There, Jesse experiences his first Freddy
possession, and he slashes his teacher to

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.840
death in the showers.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.220
Things come to a head at Lisa's pool party,
where Freddy actually bursts through Jesse's

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.820
stomach, kills his friend, and then goes after
everyone at the pool.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.390
Lisa tells Freddy that she loves Jesse and
kisses him, which prompts Freddy to burst

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.240
into flames.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.000
A Nightmare on Elm Street 3: Dream Warriors
brings Nancy back to the franchise, only now

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.600
she's an intern therapist at a psychiatric
hospital.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.400
Also at the hospital is Kristen, a teenager
who has the ability to bring other people

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.880
into her own dreams, which comes in handy
when fighting Freddy.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.800
It's during this movie that a nun named Sister
Mary Helena reveals that the only way to defeat

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:22.960
Freddy is to find his remains and bury them
on hallowed ground.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.980
Nancy becomes Freddy's final victim before
his bones are able to finally be put to rest,

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.360
destroying his monstrous form in the real
world.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.900
And how's this for a plot twist?

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.500
That helpful nun was Freddy's mom all along.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.790
A year later, in Nightmare on Elm Street 5
: The Dream Master, Dream Warrior Kristen

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:43.900
is convinced that Freddy Krueger is still
out there and looking to take down her and

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.140
her friends, since that's kind of his thing.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.960
As it turns out, he is.

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.580
After killing the other two Dream Warriors
survivors, Freddy takes aim at Kristen's new

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:57.170
friends, including a girl named Alice who
knows a powerful rhyme called "The Dream Master."

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.610
Freddy finally kills Kristen, but before she
dies, she's able to pass her dream power on

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.280
to Alice.

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:06.860
Alice confronts Freddy, and remembering "The
Dream Master" rhyme, she shows the monster

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.020
his reflection.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:09.380
"And it shall die!"

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.940
Defeated, Freddy is torn apart by the very
souls he'd trapped, releasing the ghost of

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:23.500
every trapped, murdered child.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:28.720
In Nightmare on Elm Street 5 : The Dream Child,
Alice discovers she's pregnant.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.800
But this isn't your average pregnancy.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.260
Freddy is somehow feeding her baby with the
souls of his victims.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.239
Through all of this, Alice keeps seeing a
young boy named Jacob, who turns out to be

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.440
an older version of her unborn child.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.980
Alice discovers that the body of Freddy's
mother, Amanda, is still in the asylum, and

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.340
now, the only way to defeat Freddy is to release
Amanda's soul.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.939
After a little trickery by young Dream Child
Jacob, Amanda and Jacob are able to trap Freddy's

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:56.460
soul...by turning him into an adorable baby.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:02.540
In Freddy's Dead : The Final Nightmare, a
decade has passed, and in Springwood, Ohio,

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:06.240
the entire population of minors has been mysteriously
wiped out.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:11.320
Only one remains, John Doe, who Freddy sends
out into the world in order to retrieve more

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.120
souls for him.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:17.139
Outside of the city, John comes across a youth
shelter, where he meets Maggie and a new group

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:18.519
of future victims.

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:22.049
John and Maggie have dreams involving the
same little girl, which drives them back to

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:22.660
Springwood.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:27.380
John, Maggie, and the other teens take refuge
at the old Elm Street house, where Freddy

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.360
attacks each one.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.900
Maggie eventually realizes that Freddy is
actually her father.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.840
"I know who I am."

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.620
"You're my blood.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.260
Only you could have brought me out."

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.640
With the help of another shelter employee
named Doc, it's discovered that Freddy has

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:49.340
been kept alive by dream demons, and the only
way to kill him once and for all is to drag

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.180
him into the real world.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.600
Maggie brings him into the real world and
throws a bunch of weapons at him in 3D, then

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.340
stabs him with his own glove... and blows
him up.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:03.120
In Freddy vs. Jason, it's become clear to
Freddy that the only way to make a real comeback

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:06.900
is if the teenage residents of Springwood
remember how terrifying he is.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:11.660
Freddy decides to resurrect Jason Voorhees
so the mask-wearing murderer can kill a bunch

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.000
of kids in Freddy's name.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:17.440
Things go mostly as planned as Jason goes
after local girl Lori and her friends.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:22.560
At a party in a corn field, Jason goes all
out, not only satiating his own relentless

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:26.180
desire to kill, but taking all the fun out
of it for Freddy, as well.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.380
While Lori and her friends try to figure out
a way to kill both monsters, Freddy becomes

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:33.720
increasingly more annoyed with Jason's inability
to be controlled.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:37.980
Lori figures out how to pull Freddy into the
real world, and Krueger and Voorhees face

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.840
off in the horror fight of the century.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:45.200
Wes Craven's New Nightmare isn't exactly part
of the continuity, but there are enough nods

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.660
to the original franchise that its presence
in the timeline makes sense.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:53.140
Essentially, it takes place in the real world,
and Heather Langenkamp and Robert Englund

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:57.580
play themselves, actors who've been offered
roles in a new Nightmare on Elm Street movie.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:00.840
However, the world of Nightmare starts creeping
into Heather's real life.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.680
Her sleepwalking son Dylan has dreams of Freddy.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:08.200
After he kills Heather's husband, Demon Freddy
goes after Dylan and the only person who can

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.260
stop him is Heather as Nancy.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:14.160
Heather plays the part and goes to the Elm
Street house, where Demon Freddy has Dylan

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:14.960
held captive.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:19.700
With Dylan's help, Heather eventually manages
to overpower Demon Freddy and locks him in

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.760
a furnace, where he burns to death.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:26.010
Considering that the next Nightmare film was
a full-on reboot, it looks like this death

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.320
finally took for old Freddy Krueger.

